{
  "_comment": [
    "sim/oscillator-core's graded PVT grid, expressed as a `klt sim` request.",
    "NOT RUNNABLE against klt 0.6.0 -- see klt-sim/README.md for the two",
    "reproduced blocking gaps and the upstream issue. Kept committed and",
    "current so that closing those gaps is a submit, not a rewrite.",
    "@@MODELS_DIR@@ and @@IND_MODEL@@ are the same tokens the ngspice",
    "testbench templates in ../testbench/ carry; the two generated inputs",
    "(`vco_core_body.spice`, the circuit body derived from design/vco.spice,",
    "and `corners_sg13g2.lib`, the nested-.lib aggregator that gives the",
    "single-file `models.lib` axis three families' corner sections) are",
    "produced by the reproduction recipe in README.md.",
    "Kept in step with osc_bench.sh's OSC_TSTOP / OSC_TMEAS_START: the",
    "transient is 5 ns with a 2.5 ns discard, derived from the MEASURED",
    "0.883 ns settling time, not the 20 ns design/vco.spice's comments",
    "propose. The `.meas` period count below is coarser than sim/lib.sh's",
    "osc_metrics -- TRIG/TARG RISE=n counts a FIXED number of crossings",
    "and cannot be told to count inside a time window -- so its own",
    "discarded-startup window moves with frequency. run_method_check.sh",
    "does not validate this estimator, only the one in sim/lib.sh."
  ],
  "netlist": "vco_core_body.spice",
  "netlist_source": "schematic",
  "engine": "ngspice",
  "models": {
    "lib": "corners_sg13g2.lib"
